.TH tine-export-query 1  "query " 
.SH NAME
tine\-export\-query \- Publish the pages selected by one query block UUID into published\-queries/. Sheets keep plain row outlines, as in other command\-line exports
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtine export query\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-comments\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIGRAPH\fR> <\fI((UUID))\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Publish the pages selected by one query block UUID into published\-queries/. Sheets keep plain row outlines, as in other command\-line exports
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Output name; defaults to the BEGIN_QUERY title or Query UUID
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable diagnostic logging for the desktop app
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing output, keeping the previous export in recovery
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-comments\fR
Leave comment threads out of this export
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIGRAPH\fR>

.TP
<\fI((UUID))\fR>
Persisted block UUID, bare or wrapped as ((UUID)); quote parentheses in the shell
